# Buttons: text labels only, no icons

Aura Sanctuary is a pixel-art / retro-text UI. Buttons must use text labels
only — **do not** render icon components (from `lucide-react`, etc.) inside
`<button>` elements, even as a "small visual hint" next to the label.

This applies to every interactive button rendered in the app: HUD actions,
dialog footers (Refresh, Save, Cancel), inline list actions, settings
toggles, modal close affordances — all of them. Use a clear pixel-font
label instead.

## ❌ Bad

```tsx
<button onClick={refresh}>
  <RefreshCw size={12} /> REFRESH
</button>

<button onClick={save}>
  <Save size={14} /> Save
</button>
```

## ✅ Good

```tsx
<button onClick={refresh}>REFRESH</button>

<button onClick={save}>Save</button>
```

## Notes

- Icons remain fine **outside** buttons: section headers, status chips,
  decorative tile labels (e.g. the HP/EXP/MP bars), inline list-item
  glyphs, sidebar nav links rendered as `<a>` / `<Link>`, and other
  `<Link>` elements anywhere in the app.
- If a label feels too long for its container, shorten the label (e.g.
  `ACHIEVEMENTS` → `BADGES`) rather than reaching for an icon.
- When removing an icon, also drop the now-unused `lucide-react` import
  to keep the bundle clean.

## Explicit exceptions (do NOT strip these)

The user has approved these as the only icon-in-button cases:

- **Sidebar nav buttons / links** (`src/components/aura/SideNav.tsx`
  and any sidebar-pattern usage).
- **Habitica `CONNECT` and `DISCONNECT` buttons** in
  `src/routes/settings.tsx` (the section that pairs `<Link2 />` /
  `<Link2Off />` with the label).

Everything else in any page or dialog must be text-only.
